Opt-in comparison mode for kpool-chunked-logits.diff. Apply after it.

With SGLANG_DSA_KPOOL_LOGITS_VERIFY=1, every unchunked call in
_get_topk_ragged_kpool_plan also computes the logits in seven row chunks,
compares scores (torch.equal) and top-k sets against the unchunked result and
against a second unpatched top-k run, and logs one WARNING line per call.
Off by default; with the variable unset it adds one environment lookup per call.

Diagnostic use only: it runs the logits GEMM three times, holds two
full-size logits buffers at once (the allocation the fix bounds), synchronizes
the host, and is not guarded against CUDA graph capture. Use it on short
contexts in a dedicated run. The September 27 servers carried this code with
the mode off; the September 26 check used it at 32K and 128K.

Result with kpool-chunked-logits.diff applied first: SHA-256
58e59be00ad2bec6bc28901d72c2a53853df2bc9635a9528d23528a1764a107e.

